<title>USA: Ohio unemployment falls to 4.5 pct in May.</title>
<headline>Ohio unemployment falls to 4.5 pct in May.</headline>
<dateline>COLUMBUS 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ohio's seasonally adjusted unemployment rate dropped to 4.5 percent in May from from 4.8 percent in April, the state employment services bureau reported.</p>
<p>The bureau cited stronger-than-usual seasonal hiring in recreation and entertainment-related occupations, Administrator Debra Bowland said in a statement released Friday.</p>
<p>The rate for May 1996 was 4.9 percent, the bureau noted.</p>
<p>((--David Bailey, Chicago Newsroom, 312-408-8647))</p>
